# External-model axioms (`axiom <name>`): declarations Aeneas emits in a
# generated FunsExternal.lean for a Rust function it cannot translate. They
# are the MODEL of an external, not a proof hole, and are tolerated for every
# declaration that depends on them. Each is also counted by the `axiom`
# ratchet (.axiom-ratchet), so a new one is red twice until it is named here.
#
# Rust `Iterator::fold` on a slice iterator. Emitted identically in
# generated-attenuation/PortcullisCoreAttenuation/FunsExternal.lean and
# generated-certchain/PortcullisCoreCertChain/FunsExternal.lean; the extracted
# `attenuation.chain_effective_authority` and `certchain.chain_attenuates` are
# folds over the chain. The theorems about them (AttenuationChainExtracted,
# CertChainMonotoneExtracted) are stated over the extracted functions and
# audit clean of this axiom; only the extracted bodies themselves carry it.
axiom core.slice.iter.Iter.Insts.CoreIterTraitsIteratorIteratorSharedAT.fold
